From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: taiga-expanded <taiga-expanded@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:50:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ext: curved outlines (lines, arcs, splines) drawn as one
 sketch command

New kinds profile_base, profile_boss and profile_pocket carry a closed outline
in params.outline (lines, three-point arcs, splines through points). The whole
outline is drawn by one new command, Sketcher_CreateProfile, and fixed by
Sketcher_ConstrainBlock: the model decides when and where, the runtime takes
the coordinates from the goal. The model sees a summary (segment counts, size).
Works on the XY plane, the top face, side faces and datum planes (ext.faces).
- actions: two commands appended to the catalogue (upstream ids unchanged)
- schema: three goal kinds appended; goals: three recipes
- session: create/Block branches; params: profile_pocket depth or through all
- ext/profiles.py: outline format, geometry (CCW arcs), B-spline or polyline
  splines (TAIGA_SPLINE), default outline for mistakes, shape generators
- goal encoding: outline summary (n lines/arcs/splines, width, height)
- sampler/evaluate: split and suite "outline" (bases, bosses, pockets, polar
  patterns of profiles, curved side windows)
Note: the vocabulary grows, so the published taiga-s1 weights no longer match
the patched code; evaluate them on the unpatched baseline instead.
